<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Ptolemaic Kingdom of Cyrene</h1><p class="st-meta">163 BCE – 96 BCE · capital Cyrene</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Cyrenaica as a separate Ptolemaic kingdom, created for a quarrelling royal brother and finally bequeathed to Rome.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 163 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> settled a quarrel between the brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-vi-philometor">Ptolemy VI</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-viii-physcon">Ptolemy VIII</a> by giving the younger <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> as a separate kingdom, detached from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ptolemaic-empire">Ptolemaic Empire</a>. Ptolemy VIII, nicknamed Physcon, ruled from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-cyrene">Cyrene</a> but constantly sought more, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>After an assassination attempt in 155 BCE, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-viii-physcon">Ptolemy VIII</a> published a will, preserved on a stone at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-cyrene">Cyrene</a>, leaving his kingdom to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> if he died without heirs. In 145 BCE he became king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and Cyrene was reunited with it. Around 116 BCE the kingdom was separated again for his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-apion">Ptolemy Apion</a>. The Greek cities of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pentapolis-cyrenaica">Pentapolis</a> kept their councils, and the region exported grain, horses and the last of its silphium.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-apion">Ptolemy Apion</a> died in 96 BCE and bequeathed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. The Senate left the cities free at first, then organised the province of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/roman-cyrenaica">Roman Cyrenaica</a> in 74 BCE, ending three centuries of Ptolemaic involvement in the region.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 163 BCE – 96 BCE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:56.46%;width:1.33%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>163 BCE – 96 BCE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cyrene</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ptolemy VIII, Ptolemy Apion</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ancient Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cyrenaica under Ptolemy Apion</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-130&amp;focus=ptolemaic-kingdom-of-cyrene" aria-label="Ptolemaic Kingdom of Cyrene on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5240 985 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ptolemaic Kingdom of Cyrene lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5560 1241L5772 1297M5560 1241L5632 1165"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5772 1297h0M5632 1165h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5560 1241h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5560 1241h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Cyrene. <a href="/atlas?year=-130&amp;focus=ptolemaic-kingdom-of-cyrene">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
